        body: '**Default bundle while the diagnosis clarifies:**\n- Upright positioning.\n- Oxygen target: 94-98% for most; 88-92% for hypercapnic risk.\n- Monitor, IV, ECG.\n- CXR when stable.\n- Lung/cardiac POCUS when the diagnosis is uncertain or the patient is sick.\n- VBG/ABG when ventilatory failure, severe COPD/asthma, tox, or altered mental status is possible.\n- Nebulizers if wheeze, NIV if COPD/CHF physiology and no contraindication, antibiotics if infection/sepsis, epinephrine if anaphylaxis.\n\n**Reassess every 5-15 minutes** in severe dyspnea: work of breathing, mental status, RR, ETCO2/VBG trend, oxygen requirement, and hemodynamics.\n\n**Titrate oxygen DOWN once the target is met, not just up.** Liberal oxygen raises in-hospital mortality in acutely ill adults (IOTA, 25 RCTs, RR 1.21) \u2014 leaving a patient on a non-rebreather at 100% because nobody came back to wean it is an active harm, not neutral. [30]\n\n**NIV vs HFNC vs intubation, in one line each:**\n- **CPAP/bilevel NIV** \u2014 cardiogenic pulmonary edema and hypercapnic COPD (both strong ERS/ATS recommendations); needs a cooperative patient who protects their airway. [31]\n- **HFNC** \u2014 hypoxemic (type 1) failure; endorsed in COPD by GOLD 2026 when NIV is not tolerated. Track the **ROX index** ((SpO2/FiO2)/RR): **\u22654.88** at 2/6/12 h predicts success; **<3.85** predicts intubation. [13]\n- **Intubation** \u2014 failure to protect the airway, deteriorating mental status, refractory hypoxemia, or a failed NIV trial at 1-2 hours. Device selection and titration detail: [Oxygen Delivery](#/tree/oxygen-delivery) and [HFNC](#/tree/hfnc).\n\n**Screen before you induce.** Run [HOp Killers](#/tree/hop-killers) on any dyspneic patient you are about to intubate \u2014 hypotension, hypoxemia, acidosis, and RV failure each turn a routine induction into an arrest, and severe dyspnea frequently carries more than one.',
